RUN  P01-GENERATED-BUNDLE-OFFLINE: the GENERATED bundle (object B) launches offline from its own versioned CacheStorage shell, before and after a browser restart, with the origin server stopped
RUN  P02-SW-CANNOT-SELF-UPDATE: a service worker cannot replace its own script from local objects: the update fetch bypasses the worker (served v1 from the origin although the worker would answer v2) and fails when the origin is gone; the active script stays. The worker script is therefore an immutable seed for as long as the origin server is absent
RUN  P03-STORAGE-RESTART-ORIGIN: OPFS, IndexedDB, CacheStorage and localStorage survive a browser restart on the same origin; a different port on the same host sees none of it: installed-Factory identity is the exact origin (scheme+host+port), and a moved port is a different Factory with empty storage. persisted() = false
RUN  P04-OPFS-SERVED-APP: a generated WebApp (HTML, JS modules and its wasm64 module) is served entirely from persisted OPFS objects by a service-worker router and executes the relay exactly with no origin server, before and after a browser restart (L1 primitive)
RUN  P05-SW-CROSS-ORIGIN-ISOLATION: the service-worker router can grant cross-origin isolation (COOP same-origin + COEP require-corp on synthesized navigations) with no server; SharedArrayBuffer and a shared WebAssembly.Memory become available. This removes one PRECONDITION of threaded Wasm; it does not admit threads (ERR-002/ERR-003 stay)
RUN  P06-IDB-ATOMIC-POINTER: an aborted multi-key IndexedDB transaction leaves the generation pointer untouched, and two concurrent compare-and-swap transactions from base g1 produce exactly one winner: IndexedDB can hold an atomic active/previous generation pointer and a base-unmoved ref update (the browser analogue of git update-ref <new> <old>)
GAP  P07-STORAGE-PERSISTENCE: persist() returned false in this headless, non-installed environment: the bucket stays "best-effort" and may be cleared under storage pressure (storage.bs "Storage pressure"); durability of an installed Factory's generations is not established here
RUN  P08-CANDIDATE-CONFINEMENT: an opaque-origin sandboxed iframe CANNOT reach OPFS / IndexedDB / CacheStorage / same-origin bytes (candidate code can be confined and fed only by messages); isSecureContext=true, navigator.gpu=true, memory64=true, worker=ok:object. A same-origin iframe reaches everything (opfs=opened): same-origin candidate code is NOT confined
RUN  P09-GIT-OBJECTS-IN-BROWSER: git object semantics are reproducible without the git executable: the browser recomputed every blob id and the exact HEAD tree and commit ids, inflated and verified real loose objects, built a commit byte-identical to git commit-tree, and wrote a loose object git reads
OBS  P10-KERNEL-IN-WORKER: the wasm64 kernel runs in a dedicated worker (ANALYZE status 1, BUILD status 1, diagnostics [], BUILD artifacts CANONICAL_ASCII:OK:1000 TYPED_SYSTEM_IR:OK:1486 CAPABILITY_IR:OK:1041); the wasm export surface lacks submit_contracts, submit_metrics, submit_evidence_tape, observe, read_artifact, bundle_file, so a browser host cannot supply contracts/metrics or read the emitted bundle: in-browser ASCII -> plan -> codegen -> bundle is not reachable through the current ABI [GAP]
RUN  P14-BROKEN-SW-RECOVERY: a broken service worker blocks every navigation in its scope even with the origin up; offline there is no page that can reach and unregister it; recovery needed the origin server (or browser-UI site-data clearing). The seed must be correct by construction and minimal
RUN  P16-CONFINED-GENERATION-LOAD: with the origin server stopped, a confined frame bootstrapped inline by the broker page (opaque origin, no storage, no parent DOM, no origin fetch) received its module source and wasm64 bytes only from the broker by postMessage, imported the module from a blob URL, and ran the wasm64 relay exactly. The same frame loaded by URL is not served by the SW offline (opaque-origin frames have no active service worker), so the broker must inline the bootstrap: a Factory generation can execute confined, fed exclusively by a seed-owned broker
RUN  P15-INTERRUPTED-SW-UPDATE: a service-worker update interrupted mid-install (browser closed) leaves the previous worker active after restart: the platform already gives install-or-keep-old semantics for the seed script (Install algorithm, installFailed / discarded task)
